\begin{abstract}
CCEF V4 replaces the continuum order-parameter field of V3 with a \emph{finite network of grains}. Each grain carries a qubit, whose state space $\CP^1$ is the order-parameter manifold of earlier versions, and the links between grains carry finite-dimensional gauge degrees of freedom. The connectivity of the network is itself dynamical: space is a low-temperature pattern of the network, and the Big Bang is identified with the transition into that pattern (geometrogenesis). The universe obeys a timeless global constraint; time emerges relationally (Page--Wootters), and its arrow is set by coarse-grained entropy. In the geometric phase, photons and fermions emerge from string-net condensation, Lorentz symmetry emerges approximately with a hidden preferred frame, and Einstein's equations follow from the entanglement entropy of grains, giving $G = \ell^2/4\eta_g$. The value of $G$ fixes the grain size at $\ell\simeq1.1\times10^{-35}$\,m, which matches the induced-gravity scale of V3. Poisson fluctuations in the number of grains give a dark-energy density of the observed magnitude, $\rho_\Lambda\sim H^2\Mpl^2$, that varies stochastically in time. V3 is recovered as the long-wavelength effective field theory of the geometric phase. Version~4.1 adds a protecting mechanism for emergent Lorentz invariance. A strongly coupled network flows toward a Lorentz-invariant fixed point, supplemented by emergent supersymmetry. Together these keep species-dependent speeds of light below current limits, and they place superpartners between the TeV scale and about $6\times10^{7}$\,GeV. Each statement is labelled as a postulate, an established result in the cited literature, a conjecture, or an open problem.
\end{abstract}

\paragraph{Status labels.} \st{Postulate}: assumed by CCEF. \st{Established}: a known result in the cited literature, imported here. \st{Conjecture}: a CCEF claim not yet derived. \st{Open}: an unsolved problem.

