\section{Emergent Lorentz symmetry and the hidden frame}
\label{sec:lorentz}

\paragraph{Maximum speed.} \st{Established} Any lattice system with local interactions has a maximal signal velocity, the Lieb--Robinson bound. In topologically ordered (string-net) phases it coincides with the emergent speed of light~\cite{Hamma2009}. In CCEF, $c$ is that velocity.

\paragraph{Low-energy dispersion.} For each species $a$,
\begin{equation}
E^2 = c_a^2p^2\Big[1+\xi_a^{(1)}\,\ell p+\xi_a^{(2)}\,(\ell p)^2+\cdots\Big].
\end{equation}

\noindent\textbf{Requirement 1 (no linear term).} \st{Postulate} The symmetries of the geometric phase (lattice point group together with CPT) forbid $\xi^{(1)}$. Dimension-5 Lorentz-violating operators are CPT-odd. Gamma-ray-burst timing already excludes linear dispersion beyond the Planck scale~\cite{Fermi2009,LHAASO2024}. \emph{(Corrected in V4.1.)} V4 described a quadratic term $\xi^{(2)}$ with an $O(1)$ coefficient as safe. It is not automatically safe: ultra-high-energy cosmic rays constrain it for hadrons. In V4.1 the residual Lorentz violation is set by the protecting mechanism of Section~\ref{sec:protect}, and it is much smaller.

\noindent\textbf{Requirement 2 (universal $c$).} Different species must share one limiting speed. Bounds on $|c_a-c_b|/c$ range from about $10^{-15}$ to about $10^{-23}$ depending on the species pair~\cite{ColemanGlashow1999,Mattingly2005}.

\noindent\textbf{The principal risk.} Collins \emph{et al.}~\cite{Collins2004} showed that radiative corrections generically transmit Planck-scale Lorentz violation into unsuppressed, species-dependent shifts of $c_a$, of order $\alpha/\pi$. Section~\ref{sec:protect} gives V4.1's protecting mechanism.

\paragraph{Interpretation.} The geometric phase has a rest frame: the frame of the grains. Because rulers, clocks and observers are excitations of the same network, motion through it is undetectable at low energies. This is Lorentz's interpretation of relativity, empirically equivalent to Einstein's, and it corresponds to a particular choice of the conventional one-way speed of light. \st{Conjecture} The grain frame coincides with the cosmic rest frame defined by the CMB.

